 {"id": "PEDS-U363", "ch": 46, "n": 1, "title": "DKA — Pathophysiology & Precipitants", "sec": "Pathophysiology · p213", "guide": "DKA is based on ISPAD guidelines. Severe insulin deficiency (insulinopenia) together with a rise in counter-regulatory hormones (growth hormone, glucagon, cortisol) — precipitated by infection or trauma — produces hyperglycemia with increased lipolysis: the osmotic effect of glucose causes intracellular dehydration and pseudohyponatremia, while hepatic oxidation of fatty acids forms ketone bodies (acetone, aceto-acetate, β-hydroxybutyrate) → Kussmaul breathing, abdominal pain, fruity breath.", "qs": ["PEDS-C46-001", "PEDS-C46-002", "PEDS-C46-003", "PEDS-C46-004", "PEDS-C46-005", "PEDS-C46-006", "PEDS-C46-007", "PEDS-C46-008", "PEDS-C46-009", "PEDS-C46-010", "PEDS-C46-011", "PEDS-C46-012", "PEDS-C46-013", "PEDS-C46-014", "PEDS-C46-015", "PEDS-C46-016", "PEDS-C46-017", "PEDS-C46-018", "PEDS-C46-019", "PEDS-C46-020", "PEDS-C46-021"]},
