 {"id": "PEDS-U366", "ch": 46, "n": 4, "title": "DKA — Three Pillars & Initial Management", "sec": "Management — initial management · p214", "guide": "Three pillars: correct the pathology (insulin for hyperglycemia), correct dehydration (fluid restoration), identify & treat the precipitating event (e.g. focus of infection). Minimal dehydration → oral fluids + s/c insulin. Moderate or greater dehydration → 10–20 ml/kg IV 0.9% NS over 20–30 min, insulin started after fluids as 0.05–0.1 U/kg/hr infusion → s/c on improvement. Shock → secure ABC then 20 ml/kg 0.9% NS bolus. C/I: insulin bolus (↑↑ insulin during resuscitation → cerebral edema).", "qs": ["PEDS-C46-046", "PEDS-C46-047", "PEDS-C46-048", "PEDS-C46-049", "PEDS-C46-050", "PEDS-C46-051", "PEDS-C46-052", "PEDS-C46-053", "PEDS-C46-054", "PEDS-C46-055", "PEDS-C46-056", "PEDS-C46-057", "PEDS-C46-058", "PEDS-C46-059", "PEDS-C46-060", "PEDS-C46-061", "PEDS-C46-062", "PEDS-C46-063"]},
 {"id": "PEDS-U367", "ch": 46, "n": 5, "title": "DKA — Further Management & Complications", "sec": "Further management · p214", "guide": "Cerebral edema → slow deficit correction over 24–48 hr. Insulin-induced hypokalemia → NS + 40 mEq/L KCl; bicarbonate therapy is contraindicated (worsens CNS acidosis & hypokalemia). Blood glucose < 300 mg/dl → add 5% dextrose to IV fluids to prevent hypoglycemia. Hypernatremia restores on treating the hyperglycemia.", "qs": ["PEDS-C46-064", "PEDS-C46-065", "PEDS-C46-066", "PEDS-C46-067", "PEDS-C46-068", "PEDS-C46-069", "PEDS-C46-070", "PEDS-C46-071", "PEDS-C46-072", "PEDS-C46-073", "PEDS-C46-074", "PEDS-C46-075", "PEDS-C46-076", "PEDS-C46-077", "PEDS-C46-078"]},
