 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "Which feature places a DKA child in the \"moderate or greater dehydration\" column?", "opts": ["Intolerant to oral fluids", "Tolerating oral fluids well", "Pitting pedal oedema", "Polyuria with thirst only"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Moderate column: not in shock, intolerant to oral fluids, symptoms of dehydration with vomiting. (Book p214)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C46-052"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "True or False — In moderate dehydration, the insulin infusion is started before the fluid bolus.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — insulin is started AFTER the fluid therapy. (Book p214)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C46-053"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "The IV insulin infusion rate used in DKA is —", "opts": ["0.01–0.05 U/kg/hr", "0.5–1 U/kg/hr", "0.05–0.1 U/kg/hr", "0.1–0.2 U/kg/hr"], "ans": 2, "exp": "IV insulin infusion 0.05–0.1 U/kg/hr, converted to s/c insulin upon improvement. (Book p214)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C46-054"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "True or False — Once the child improves, the intravenous insulin infusion in DKA is converted to subcutaneous insulin.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — the algorithm shows IV infusion → s/c insulin upon improvement. (Book p214)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C46-055"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "The features that define shock in a child with DKA are —", "opts": ["Thready pulses with ↓ consciousness or coma", "Tolerating oral fluids with mild thirst", "Vomiting with normal sensorium", "Deep breathing with normal pulses"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Shock column: thready pulses, decreased consciousness or coma. (Book p214)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C46-056"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "In DKA with shock, after securing airway, breathing and circulation, the fluid step is —", "opts": ["Oral rehydration solution by nasogastric tube", "IV bolus of 20 ml/kg of 0.9% NS", "IV bolus of 10 ml/kg of 0.45% NS", "IV insulin bolus 0.1 U/kg"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Shock: 20 ml/kg IV bolus of 0.9% NS. (Book p214)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C46-057"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "True or False — An insulin bolus given during DKA resuscitation increases the risk of cerebral edema.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — C/I: insulin bolus (↑↑ insulin during resuscitation → cerebral edema). (Book p214)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C46-058"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "Match the DKA presentation with the correct initial step:", "opts": ["A-1, B-2, C-3, D-4", "A-2, B-3, C-1, D-4", "A-4, B-3, C-2, D-1", "A-2, B-1, C-3, D-4"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Correct pairs: Minimal dehydration→Oral fluids; Moderate or greater dehydration→10–20 ml/kg IV NS over 20–30 min; Shock→20 ml/kg IV bolus 0.9% NS after securing ABC; Insulin route in minimal dehydration→Subcutaneous. (Book p214)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Minimal dehydration", "Subcutaneous"], ["Moderate or greater dehydration", "20 ml/kg IV bolus 0.9% NS after securing ABC"], ["Shock", "10–20 ml/kg IV NS over 20–30 min"], ["Insulin route in minimal dehydration", "Oral fluids"]], "id": "PEDS-C46-059"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "A 5-year-old with DKA is drowsy with thready pulses and capillary refill of 4 seconds; glucose 520 mg/dl.", "opts": ["Secure ABC and give 20 ml/kg IV bolus of 0.9% NS", "Give an IV insulin bolus 0.1 U/kg", "Give IV sodium bicarbonate 1 mEq/kg", "Start oral rehydration solution via nasogastric tube"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Shock in DKA → airway, breathing, circulation secured + 20 ml/kg 0.9% NS bolus; insulin bolus is contraindicated. (Book p214)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 5-year-old with DKA is drowsy, has thready pulses and capillary refill of 4 seconds; blood glucose is 520 mg/dl.", "id": "PEDS-C46-060"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "A 12-year-old with DKA (pH 7.28, bicarbonate 16 mmol/l) is alert, taking sips and has minimal dehydration.", "opts": ["Nil orally with 0.45% saline at twice maintenance", "Oral fluids with subcutaneous insulin", "20 ml/kg NS bolus followed by insulin infusion", "IV insulin infusion 0.1 U/kg/hr alone"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Minimal dehydration with tolerated oral fluids → oral fluids + subcutaneous insulin, no IV bolus needed. (Book p214)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 12-year-old with DKA (venous pH 7.28, bicarbonate 16 mmol/l) is alert, tolerating oral fluids and has minimal dehydration.", "id": "PEDS-C46-061"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "A 9-year-old in DKA has moderate dehydration with vomiting and is intolerant to oral fluids, but is not in shock.", "opts": ["IV insulin infusion first, then 10 ml/kg NS over 2 hours", "5% dextrose with 40 mEq/L KCl as the first fluid", "10–20 ml/kg IV 0.9% NS over 20–30 minutes, then insulin infusion", "20 ml/kg IV NS bolus repeated twice, then oral fluids"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Moderate dehydration: 10–20 ml/kg IV NS over 20–30 min, with insulin infusion (0.05–0.1 U/kg/hr) started after the fluid therapy. (Book p214)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 9-year-old in DKA has moderate dehydration with vomiting, is intolerant to oral fluids, and is not in shock.", "id": "PEDS-C46-062"},
 {"sec": "DKA initial management", "page": 214, "q": "Odd one out (steps correctly used in the initial management of DKA):", "opts": ["10–20 ml/kg 0.9% NS over 20–30 min", "20 ml/kg 0.9% NS bolus in shock", "Insulin infusion 0.05–0.1 U/kg/hr after fluids", "IV insulin bolus before fluids"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Insulin bolus is contraindicated in DKA (↑ cerebral edema risk); the other three are the book's initial steps. (Book p214)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C46-063"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "Cerebral edema during DKA therapy is prevented by —", "opts": ["Slow deficit correction over 24–48 hr", "Rapid correction of the deficit in 6–12 hr", "Early insulin bolus", "Bicarbonate infusion"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Cerebral edema → slow deficit correction over 24–48 hr. (Book p214)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C46-064"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "In DKA, the fluid deficit should be corrected slowly over ___ hours.", "opts": ["12–18", "24–48", "6–12", "48–72"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Deficit correction is spread over 24–48 hours. (Book p214)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C46-065"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "Insulin-induced hypokalemia during DKA therapy is managed by using —", "opts": ["0.45% saline with no potassium", "Ringer lactate with 10 mEq/L KCl", "NS + 40 mEq/L of KCl", "5% dextrose with 20 mEq/L KCl"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Insulin-induced hypokalemia → NS + 40 mEq/L of KCl used. (Book p214)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C46-066"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "The potassium concentration added to NS during DKA management is ___ mEq/L of KCl.", "opts": ["20", "60", "10", "40"], "ans": 3, "exp": "NS + 40 mEq/L KCl. (Book p214)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C46-067"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "True or False — Bicarbonate therapy in DKA is contraindicated because it worsens CNS acidosis and hypokalemia.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — C/I to bicarbonate: worsening of CNS acidosis and hypokalemia. (Book p214)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C46-068"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "Bicarbonate is avoided in DKA because it —", "opts": ["Blocks insulin receptor signalling", "Worsens CNS acidosis and hypokalemia", "Causes hypernatremia with seizures", "Directly raises intracranial pressure"], "ans": 1, "exp": "The book's contraindication is worsening of CNS acidosis and hypokalemia. (Book p214)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C46-069"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "When blood glucose falls below ___ mg/dl in DKA, 5% dextrose is added to the IV fluids.", "opts": ["250", "150", "300", "200"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Glucose < 300 mg/dl → add 5% dextrose to IV fluids. (Book p214)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C46-070"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "The purpose of adding 5% dextrose to the IV fluids during DKA therapy is —", "opts": ["To accelerate insulin action", "To correct hypernatremia", "To replace potassium losses", "To prevent hypoglycemia"], "ans": 3, "exp": "5% dextrose is added (once glucose < 300 mg/dl) to prevent hypoglycemia. (Book p214)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C46-071"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "Hypernatremia that develops during DKA management —", "opts": ["Restores on treating the hyperglycemia", "Requires 0.45% saline", "Needs free-water restriction", "Responds to desmopressin"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Hypernatremia restores on treating hyperglycemia. (Book p214)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C46-072"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "True or False — Hypernatremia complicating DKA needs specific therapy with hypotonic fluids.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — it restores on treating the hyperglycemia. (Book p214)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C46-073"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "Match the DKA problem with its management:", "opts": ["A-1, B-4, C-2, D-3", "A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1", "A-4, B-3, C-2, D-1", "A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Correct pairs: Cerebral edema→Slow deficit correction over 24–48 hr; Insulin-induced hypokalemia→NS + 40 mEq/L KCl; Blood glucose < 300 mg/dl→Add 5% dextrose to IV fluids; Hypernatremia→Restores on treating hyperglycemia. (Book p214)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Cerebral edema", "Restores on treating hyperglycemia"], ["Insulin-induced hypokalemia", "Slow deficit correction over 24–48 hr"], ["Blood glucose < 300 mg/dl", "NS + 40 mEq/L KCl"], ["Hypernatremia", "Add 5% dextrose to IV fluids"]], "id": "PEDS-C46-074"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "A 6-year-old on the DKA protocol develops headache and drowsiness 8 hours after starting therapy; glucose is 250 mg/dl.", "opts": ["Hypoglycemia", "Hypernatremia", "Hypokalemia", "Cerebral edema"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Cerebral edema appears during therapy (avoid rapid correction/insulin bolus) → slow deficit correction over 24–48 hr. (Book p214)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 6-year-old treated for DKA becomes drowsy with headache 8 hours after fluids and insulin were started; blood glucose is 250 mg/dl.", "id": "PEDS-C46-075"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "A child on DKA treatment develops flaccid weakness and shallow breathing; serum potassium is 2.6 mEq/l.", "opts": ["Add 40 mEq/L of KCl to the NS infusion", "Give an insulin bolus to shift potassium intracellularly", "Switch to 0.45% saline without potassium", "Give sodium bicarbonate for the acidosis"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Insulin-induced hypokalemia → NS with 40 mEq/L KCl; bicarbonate is contraindicated. (Book p214)", "type": "case", "stem": "A child receiving insulin for DKA develops flaccid weakness and shallow breathing; serum potassium is 2.6 mEq/l.", "id": "PEDS-C46-076"},
 {"sec": "DKA further management", "page": 214, "q": "True or False — The fluid deficit in DKA should be replaced as rapidly as possible to avoid cerebral edema.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — rapid correction causes cerebral edema; slow deficit correction over 24–48 hr is advised. (Book p214)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C46-077"},
